   "title": "Boeing, 717 Airplane Characteristics for Airport Planning (D6-58330 Rev B, November 2014), 2.2 General Dimensions, 2.3 Ground Clearances, 2.7.1 Forward and Aft Cargo Door Clearances, 2.7.2 Door Clearances: Model 717-200",
   "accessed": "2026-11-15",
   "note": "Dimensions and outlines read off the side, plan and front views of 2.2 (tools/trace/b712/); the figures are the aircraft's measurements, not a copy of the drawing. A T-tail (the tailplane on the fin's top) and two BR715 nacelles on the rear fuselage, each on a stub pylon. The sheet draws the cabin windows and the left side's doors: the main entry door sits within 1 cm of 2.7.2's printed 4.38 m to its middle. The right side's service door is placed from 2.7.2's partial plan (its opening 4.14-4.84 m from the nose, 27.3 in wide, 48.5 in tall, its sill with the main door's). The cargo doors (on the right) are at 2.7.1's table (9.94 m and 24.56 m to their middles); the sheet draws the forward one 0.28 m aft of that, the aft one 0.14 m. Heights above the crown are checked against 2.3's ground clearances, each the middle of its range (the aircraft's attitudes and loads) less the crown's: good to about 0.15 m. The plan prints the engine 3.30 m (10 ft 10 in) from the centerline, where both the plan and the front view draw the nacelle's middle at 2.87 m, the nacelle as wide as printed (1.94 m against 1.93) and 0.25 m clear of the fuselage; the shape keeps the drawing's (−13%)."
  }
